<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine first half trade deficit $5.631 bln. [CORRECTED 03:20 GMT]</title>
<headline>Philippine first half trade deficit $5.631 bln. [CORRECTED 03:20 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine trade deficit fell to $5.631 billion (corrects by inserting dropped word billion) in the first six months of the year from $6.047 billion registered in the same period last year, the National Statistics Office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan-June 97    Jan-May 97   Jan-June 96</p>
<p>    Exports		   11.700	9.571	 9.582</p>
<p>    Imports		   17.331     14.296	15.629</p>
<p>    Trade balance	  -5.631	-4.725	-6.047</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billion dollars</p>
<p>The June trade deficit reached $906 million from $957 million in the same month last year.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE	June 97	May 97	June 96</p>
<p>    Exports		    2.129	   1.983	 1.793</p>
<p>    Imports		    3.035	   2.954	 2.750</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -0.906	  -0.971	-0.957</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billion dollars</p>
